    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0522" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/817: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Damm</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-26T12:00:00-06:00">April 26,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>From Guaymas:</p>
                <p>“Urgent for Department. April 26, 10 a.m. Eaton<anchor n="61" xml:id="d484-f1"/>
                    reports Federals bomb dropped through roof of his office yesterday without
                    injury to him but some material damage. I have telegraphed to General Calles and
                    requested that orders be given to prevent repetition of the incident. Eaton also
                    reports rebel retreat under way with destination reported to be Guaymas. Present
                    whereabouts retreating rebels unknown due to the interruption of
                    communications”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Damm</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d484-f1" n="61" xml:id="d484-f1-content">
                <p>Vice Consul in charge at Ciudad Obregon.</p>
